# Suppresses a single, pre-existing, unrelated LeakSanitizer report that only
# OPCUA_LocalHandlerStartServerRace hits, because no other systemtest uses the "-d OPCUA_DEV"
# device. All 34 allocations in that report originate from OPCUA_MGR::initialize() (called from
# OPCUA_DEV::startDevice()), via two different sub-paths -- addMethodNode() (once per management
# method OPCUA_MGR registers) and addMgmtObjectInstance() -- each leaking a small array/string
# inside open62541's node-copy machinery. Matching on OPCUA_MGR::initialize(), the single entry
# point both sub-paths share, rather than on the far more generic open62541 helper UA_Array_copy
# they eventually reach, keeps this from also silencing an unrelated leak that happens to pass
# through that same generic helper from a completely different, unrelated caller. This is not a
# process-wide leak-detection disable -- a genuinely new leak elsewhere is still caught. See the
# comment next to OPCUA_LocalHandlerStartServerRace in CMakeLists.txt, and
# https://github.com/eclipse-4diac/4diac-forte/issues/1054 for the leak itself.
leak:OPCUA_MGR::initialize
